WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.100
Three phones run the NearbyChat sample.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.300
The advertiser starts advertising.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.000
The discoverers start discovering and find it.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.400
A discoverer asks to connect. The advertiser accepts the request.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:26.300
The other discoverer asks to connect and is accepted too.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.300
All three are connected. Every connection is encrypted.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:42.800
Each phone stops advertising or discovering. The connections stay up.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:49.100
Each side opens its chat. Each pair of phones derived the same six-digit authentication code on its own.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:55.100
Al's S22 and Bill's S21 confirm their code matches. Jay's S24 keeps its code up until its turn.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:03.300
Al's S22 sends Bill's S21 a text message.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:14.100
Then a photo, sent as a file.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:20.800
Al's S22 closes that chat and opens the one with Jay's S24. This pair shows its own code.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.900
Both confirm the code matches.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:33.500
Now Jay's S24 sends Al's S22 a text.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:52.700
Then the video: three and a half minutes of Big Buck Bunny, about 100 MB, phone to phone.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:02:06.166
Bill's S21 disconnects, then Jay's S24. Every phone's connections page empties.

